# PLANK Output

The operator requested a named macOS playback destination because the selected
physical speaker name obscures remote playback. Work stays on the native media
feature branch; Host deployment remains macOS27/SDK27.

Publish a real output-only Audio Server Plug-in device named PLANK Output,
48kHz stereo Float32 with volume/mute controls. Its final mix is a silent sink.
Use a Core Audio tap restricted to that output's stream and the admitted user's
processes. The operator explicitly requested ordinary local playback for all
physical outputs. Use CATapUnmuted: only audio routed to PLANK Output is forwarded.
Preserve active-user admission, system-alert validation, capture consent,
and the single Opus/Kymux media path.
There is no public loopback input, PCM capture in root, second encoder or new
network feature schema. Tap gain applies PLANK Output's controls once, independently
of the current default device. A newly selected output
inherits the prior master volume/mute (or the lower channel gain when no master
exists); subsequent changes leave physical controls untouched.

After desktop audio is active, the signed admitted worker requests a renewable
local routing lease from the root coordinator. The coordinator records stable
UIDs for playback and system-alert defaults in the private OutputRouting directory
created by the installer beneath the shared settings folder, before
selecting PLANK Output. No route change occurs before consent or for LoginWindow.
Driver absence or incompatible format disables desktop audio without capturing
physical outputs. Automatic-routing failure permits explicit PLANK Output selection.

Normal disconnect, worker loss, expired heartbeat and graphical revocation
restore owned defaults. A manual replacement wins. If an original device was
unplugged, use an available built-in output; never guess an external replacement.
HAL failure preserves the journal and retries off the authentication queue.
Coordinator abnormal exit triggers launchd restart and journal recovery.
Explicitly user-selected PLANK defaults are not owned or undone by the session.

Validate driver format/control/IO bounds, gain handling, real journal recovery,
partial selection, manual override, missing devices and malformed/unauthorized
local XPC. Run existing tap/recovery/session and packaging gates. Deliver a new
signed candidate with the native deferrable restart recommendation. Live gates:
Sound Settings output selection, volume/mute, app and alert delivery, app-pinned
outputs, connect/disconnect, worker/coordinator crash, unplug, and stereo checks.
Component tests do not establish installed driver or application acceptance.
